$DIR/test.p:5:4: no new variables on left side of :=
    x := v declares new variables. Every name on the left already exists in this
    scope, so nothing would be declared. Use = to assign to the existing
    variables.
    (see "Short variable declarations" in the Plutonium spec, section 10.11)
    (run "pluto explain E0019" for a longer explanation)

$DIR/test.p:4:2: declared and not used: x
    x is declared on line 4, but its value is never used. Plutonium, like Go,
    treats this as an error, because an unused variable often means a mistake,
    such as assigning to the wrong variable or forgetting a check.
    Delete the variable, use it, or replace it with _ where it is declared if
    you only need the other values.
    To keep it for now:
        _ = x
    (see "Variable declarations" in the Plutonium spec, section 10.10)
    (run "pluto explain E0101" for a longer explanation)
